 "description": "The card for one film on one board: title, year, runtime, genres, directors, cast, overview, rating, a trailer url and a TMDB poster url when present, its upcoming showtimes nearest first with venue/time/ticket link, and a last-night flag when the run is ending. Returns the 40 nearest showtimes (\"concise\") or up to 200 (\"detailed\"); showtime_count is the total and showtimes_complete says whether the list is whole \u2014 scenef_search_showtimes with a date or theater narrows the rest. Read-only: the call itself records nothing. SceneF does not sell, hold or book tickets. Ticket links are https://scenef.com/go/{id} redirects to the theater's own site or the ticket seller it uses (a link to a showtime that is gone lands back on SceneF); whoever follows one, a person or a client, is logged once anonymously (time, the screening with its film and theater, client type, browser family, referring site, link source tag, and whether the showtime was gone; no IP address, cookie or account) and forwarded. Every emitted showtime carries confidence, source tier, reporting sources and verified_at.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "film": {
    "description": "Film title or SceneF slug.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "region": {
    "description": "Which regional board to read: a board id such as \"sf\", \"oahu\" or \"miami\", not a city name (\"Honolulu\" or \"Chicago\" is rejected). Omitted means \"sf\" (San Francisco); it is never inferred from where you are. For a city, ZIP or neighborhood call scenef_resolve_board first; scenef_now with no region lists every id. An unknown region is an error, not a fallback.",
    "maxLength": 120,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "response_format": {
    "description": "Output size. \"concise\" (default) is tight text plus a structured summary. In whats_playing, each film has the total showtime_count, next_showtime, and a showtimes array containing only that next screening; \"detailed\" adds showtime rows with ids, ticket urls and accuracy metadata, about 200 across the answer. film_details and search_showtimes return the 40 nearest showtimes in \"concise\" and up to 200 in \"detailed\". showtime_count is always the total and showtimes_complete says whether the array is all of it; narrow by date or theater for the rest.",
    "enum": [
     "concise",
     "detailed"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "film"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
